\ Convert an existing native year candidate into its wide equivalent.
\ This adapter is for differential checks and incremental migration.
\ Both absolute boundary days and gate indices are signed-wide fields;
\ day length and span count are recomputed, not copied on faith.
\ Only conversion-safe native integers may be passed. The full date
\ entrypoint already enforces a stricter native-safe coordinate bound.
\ A failed field conversion leaves the adapter's success flag zero.
\ This is not yet a wide year-discovery algorithm.

The widened year conversion succeeded is a number.

To copy a year candidate into a wide year candidate:
  Put 0 into the widened year conversion succeeded.
  Convert the year candidate's opening day into a wide signed day.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1, exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide year candidate's opening day.
  Convert the year candidate's closing day into a wide signed day.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1, exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide year candidate's closing day.
  Convert the year candidate's opening index into a wide signed day.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1, exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide year candidate's opening index.
  Convert the year candidate's closing index into a wide signed day.
  If the native widening succeeded is not 1, exit.
  Put the converted signed day result into the wide year candidate's closing index.
  Measure the wide year candidate.
  Put 1 into the widened year conversion succeeded.
